:       PersistentVolumeClaim (a reference to a PersistentVolumeClaim in the same namespace)\n    ClaimName:  geo-pvc-broken\n    ReadOnly:   false\n  init-script:\n    Type:      ConfigMap (a volume populated by a ConfigMap)\n    Name:      mongo-geo-script\n    Optional:  false\n  failure-script:\n    Type:      ConfigMap (a volume populated by a ConfigMap)\n    Name:      failure-admin-geo\n    Optional:  false\n  kube-api-access-z4z8r:\n    Type:                    Projected (a volume that contains injected data from multiple sources)\n    TokenExpirationSeconds:  3607\n    ConfigMapName:           kube-root-ca.crt\n    Optional:                false\n    DownwardAPI:             true\nQoS Class:                   Burstable\nNode-Selectors:              <none>\nTolerations:                 node.kubernetes.io/not-ready:NoExecute op=Exists for 300s\n                             node.kubernetes.io/unreachable:NoExecute op=Exists for 300s\nEvents:\n  Type     Reason            Age                From               Message\n  ----     ------            ----               ----               -------\n  Warning  FailedScheduling  67s (x4 over 78s)  default-scheduler  0/3 nodes are available: persistentvolumeclaim "geo-pvc-broken" not found. preemption: 0/3 nodes are available: 3 Preemption is not helpful for scheduling.\n', id='835faaa5-dc6e-41f7-99c7-17bc7e8a034a', tool_call_id='chatcmpl-tool-ad5c7cb82e3991c1'), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='59d3b367-5fed-43c1-87bc-aceb41a85bb9'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let\'s see. The user is trying to diagnose why the MongoDB Geo pod is in a Pending state. From the previous steps, we know that the pod can\'t be scheduled because the PersistentVolumeClaim (PVC) "geo-pvc-broken" isn\'t found. The error message from the describe pod command clearly states that the PVC is missing.\n\nSo, the next logical step is to check if the PVC exists. The PVC is supposed to provide the storage for the MongoDB instance. If it\'s not found, the pod can\'t mount the volume, leading to scheduling failure. \n\nThe tool available for this is exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd. The command would be to get the PVCs in the namespace. By running "kubectl get pvc -n hotel-reservation", we can verify if "geo-pvc-broken" is present. If it\'s not there, that\'s the root cause—the PVC wasn\'t created, maybe due to a typo, misconfiguration, or a missing storage class. \n\nAlternatively, if the PVC exists but is in a different state, that\'s another issue. But the immediate problem here is the absence of the PVC. So checking the PVC list is the next step to confirm this.\n</think>\n\ntool name: exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd  \nreasoning: The MongoDB Geo pod is pending due to a missing PersistentVolumeClaim (PVC) "geo-pvc-broken." To confirm this, I need to check if the PVC exists in the namespace. If it\'s missing, the root cause is likely a failed PVC creation (e.g., typo, misconfiguration, or storage class issues).  \n\n<tool_call>  \n{"name": "exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd", "arguments": {"command": "kubectl get pvc -n hotel-reservation"}}  \n</tool_call>', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 368, 'prompt_tokens': 5308, 'total_tokens': 5676, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfcc7-b640-7a13-a27b-93321c62e6a9-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 5308, 'output_tokens': 368, 'total_tokens': 5676}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='cdd81a08-8004-4158-b646-d728ca0731ba'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let\'s see. The user is trying to figure out why the MongoDB Geo pod is pending. From the previous steps, we found that the pod is waiting because the PVC "geo-pvc-broken" isn\'t found. So the next logical step is to check if that PVC actually exists in the namespace.\n\nI need to use the kubectl command to list all PVCs in the hotel-reservation namespace. The command would be "kubectl get pvc -n hotel-reservation". This will show all the PVCs and their statuses. If "geo-pvc-broken" isn\'t listed, then we know the PVC is missing, which points to a problem in the PVC creation process. \n\nPossible reasons for the missing PVC could be a typo in the PVC name, a misconfiguration in the storage class, or maybe the PVC wasn\'t created at all. Once we confirm the PVC is missing, the next step would be to check the PVC\'s definition, maybe look at the deployment or stateful set that references it, and see why it wasn\'t provisioned. But first, we need to verify the existence of the PVC. So the tool call should be to get the PVCs in the namespace.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl get pvc -n hotel-reservation"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-8630b55e4cbfb3b2', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 281, 'prompt_tokens': 6327, 'total_tokens': 6608, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfcc7-c7ec-7172-bd7f-a734c2a2e13c-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl get pvc -n hotel-reservation'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-8630b55e4cbfb3b2', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 6327, 'output_tokens': 281, 'total_tokens': 6608}), ToolMessage(content='NAME                 STATUS   VOLUME                                     CAPACITY   ACCESS MODES   STORAGECLASS       VOLUMEATTRIBUTESCLASS   AGE\ngeo-pvc              Bound    pvc-d7163482-e722-4b68-9dfd-e44aecd2c095   1Gi        RWO            openebs-hostpath   <unset>                 2m55s\nprofile-pvc          Bound    pvc-c51a4787-cfb0-49cf-962e-c35799efebda   1Gi        RWO            openebs-hostpath   <unset>                 2m46s\nrate-pvc             Bound    pvc-acc3aad0-8b2e-480a-af6c-8262701823ad   1Gi        RWO            openebs-hostpath   <unset>                 2m39s\nrecommendation-pvc   Bound    pvc-f5bf4656-b853-4805-9523-dfec45f25a73   1Gi        RWO            openebs-hostpath   <unset>                 2m35s\nreservation-pvc      Bound    pvc-e27ebfaa-2a40-486c-bf4a-cb212a0ad11e   1Gi        RWO            openebs-hostpath   <unset>                 2m29s\nuser-pvc             Bound    pvc-343f3e88-cf45-4424-9000-cf5035fe2563   1Gi        RWO            openebs-hostpath   <unset>                 2m18s\n', id='9994be20-7b1e-474b-8e18-1836dca3ba8e', tool_call_id='chatcmpl-tool-8630b55e4cbfb3b2'), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='a067209f-b52c-41ef-b813-23bbf7080c56'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let\'s see. The user is trying to figure out why the MongoDB Geo pod is pending. From the previous steps, we found that the pod is waiting for a PVC called "geo-pvc-broken", but when we checked the PVCs in the namespace, there\'s a PVC named "geo-pvc" that\'s bound. The error message mentioned "persistentvolumeclaim "geo-pvc-broken" not found," which suggests there\'s a mismatch between the PVC name expected by the pod and the actual PVC name in the cluster.\n\nSo, the next step is to check the deployment or statefulset configuration for the MongoDB Geo service. The deployment might be referencing