 the wrong PVC name, maybe a typo or a misconfiguration. The user needs to verify the PVC name specified in the deployment\'s YAML file. If the deployment is using "geo-pvc-broken" but the actual PVC is "geo-pvc", that\'s the root cause. \n\nThe tool to use here is `exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd` with the command `kubectl get deployment mongodb-geo -n hotel-reservation -o yaml` to inspect the deployment\'s configuration. This will show the PVC details referenced in the deployment. Once we see the incorrect PVC name, we can confirm the typo and suggest correcting it to match the existing "geo-pvc".\n</think>\n\ntool name: exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd  \nreasoning: The PVC "geo-pvc-broken" referenced in the MongoDB Geo pod\'s configuration does not exist, but a PVC named "geo-pvc" is present and bound. This indicates a typo or misconfiguration in the deployment\'s PVC reference. To confirm, I need to inspect the MongoDB Geo deployment\'s YAML configuration to verify the exact PVC name being requested.  \n\n<tool_call>  \n{"name": "exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd", "arguments": {"command": "kubectl get deployment mongodb-geo -n hotel-reservation -o yaml"}}  \n</tool_call>', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 399, 'prompt_tokens': 5923, 'total_tokens': 6322, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfcc7-d855-7222-969b-3ef98955d4f1-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 5923, 'output_tokens': 399, 'total_tokens': 6322}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='6f93f819-75e2-4763-829a-0fb90611f90b'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let\'s see. The user is trying to figure out why the MongoDB Geo